"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdoc_crossplaycore=self.webpackChunkdoc_crossplaycore||[]).push([[3361],{4782:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"1-2-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/changelog/1-2-0","source":"@site/changelog/2026-11-26-1-2-0/index.md","title":"CrossplayCore 1.2.0","description":"ADDED","date":"2026-11-26T22:09:30.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"CrossplayCore 1.2.0","slug":"1-2-0","date":"2026-11-26T22:09:30"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"CrossplayCore 1.1.0","permalink":"/changelog/1-1-0"}},"content":"## ADDED\\n\\n- Added the **Block Lobby Requests When Sanctions Unknown** setting, which rejects lobby requests when the login sanctions check cannot determine the player\'s sanctions.\\n\\n## CHANGED\\n\\n- Enabled Online Subsystem Steam and Steam Sockets as plugin dependencies on Windows, Linux, and macOS.\\n- Lobby update operations now report failures returned by Steam or Epic Online Services (EOS) to the caller.\\n- Added a Crossplay Blueprint example to the sample project.\\n\\n## FIXED\\n\\n- Fixed a race condition when destroying a session while a create, join, or update operation was still in progress. Session destruction now waits for the active operation to finish.\\n- Fixed pending login retries continuing after logout.\\n- Improved how Steam and EOS callbacks handle login, lobby membership, and session state changes.\\n- Fixed the same player\'s crossplay user IDs comparing as different when only one of them had a Product User Id.\\n- Fixed **Is Lobby Owner** returning true for a lobby without a valid owner.\\n- Fixed Crossplay Online Subsystem user IDs not converting correctly to and from bytes.\\n- Presence queries for known friends now return the cached presence immediately."},{"id":"1-1-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/changelog/1-1-0","source":"@site/changelog/2026-11-26-1-1-0/index.md","title":"CrossplayCore 1.1.0","description":"ADDED","date":"2026-11-26T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"CrossplayCore 1.1.0","slug":"1-1-0"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"CrossplayCore 1.2.0","permalink":"/changelog/1-2-0"},"nextItem":{"title":"CrossplayCore 1.0.0","permalink":"/changelog/1-0-0"}},"content":"## ADDED\\n\\n- Added stats, leaderboards, and achievement progress APIs for Steam and EOS, available through Blueprint and the Crossplay Online Subsystem.\\n- Added Quick Match, which looks for a lobby to join and creates one if no suitable lobby is available.\\n- Added platform restrictions for lobbies and an option to prevent players from joining a match in progress.\\n- Added lobby management and social APIs for updating lobby settings, kicking players, sending lobby chat messages, ending matches, and accessing avatars and recent players.\\n- Added EOS player reports, sanctions checks, and friend requests. Configured sanctions can block lobby creation, joining, and Quick Match.\\n\\n## FIXED\\n\\n- Fixed an issue where two players using Quick Match at the same time could create separate lobbies and remain split.\\n- Lobby creation, joining, and Quick Match now wait for the initial EOS sanctions check when lobby-blocking sanctions are configured.\\n- Successful lobby settings updates are now reflected immediately in the current lobby.\\n- Logging out now cancels pending login and lobby requests while preserving EOS logins managed by other plugins."},{"id":"1-0-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/changelog/1-0-0","source":"@site/changelog/2026-11-07-1-0-0/index.md","title":"CrossplayCore 1.0.0","description":"First release of CrossplayCore.","date":"2026-11-07T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"CrossplayCore 1.0.0","slug":"1-0-0"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"CrossplayCore 1.1.0","permalink":"/changelog/1-1-0"}},"content":"First release of CrossplayCore.\\n\\n## ADDED\\n\\n- Added the CrossplayCore module with Steam and Epic Online Services (EOS) backends and Blueprint nodes for login, lobbies, friends, invites, presence, and matches.\\n- Added login with Steam through EOS Connect, Epic account login (Never, Launcher Only, or Always), optional Steam-to-Epic account linking with a Steam-only fallback, and Dev Auth Tool login for testing several players in PIE.\\n- Added typed lobby and member attributes with search filters for EOS and Steam lobbies.\\n- Added Steam lobbies, used when the lobby service is Platform Only or EOS is not available.\\n- Added match start over EOS P2P and Steam P2P, with lobby members traveling to the owner\'s match address.\\n- Added lobby invites, offline invites, Steam game invites, and joining from the Steam overlay, accepted EOS invites, or the `+crossplay_lobby` and `+connect_lobby` launch arguments. Pending joins are kept until login completes.\\n- Added the Epic friends overlay for lobby invites, with the Steam invite dialog as a fallback.\\n- Added Epic and Steam friends with Product User Id lookup, presence and rich presence text, and friend update and removal events.\\n- Added EOS lobby voice chat with Blueprint controls for muting, volume, and audio devices, and Online Subsystem voice chat for matches when lobby voice is unavailable.\\n- Added EOS achievement unlocking.\\n- Added the Crossplay Online Subsystem (`CROSSPLAY`) with Identity, Sessions, Friends, Presence, and Achievements, so the built-in session Blueprint nodes work on top of CrossplayCore.\\n- Added a host migration adapter for HostMigrationCore.\\n- Added support for the EOSCore and SteamCore PRO platforms and networking, including SteamCoreSockets.\\n- Added an option to use the EOS sandbox and deployment IDs supplied by the Epic Games launcher.\\n- Added configurable EOS friends and presence scopes.\\n- Added a setting that allows players whose net IDs come from another Online Subsystem to join crossplay matches.\\n\\n## FIXED\\n\\n- Fixed `OnLobbyMemberJoined` firing before the member\'s display name had arrived.\\n- Fixed Steam lobby joining by dispatching Steam callbacks to the game thread and keeping the platform user ID when the crossplay login fails.\\n- Steam lobby joins are now accepted when the Steam user is available, even if the EOS login fails.\\n- Lobbies and matches now recover after a process was killed and left its EOS lobby membership behind. Create and Join are refused while another lobby request is running.\\n- Host migration now detects a host that left the lobby, ignores host announcements from an earlier process, and no longer joins a match address that points at the local player.\\n- The current lobby is left when the subsystem shuts down.\\n- The game net driver is restored after a match, and a surviving EOS socket subsystem is registered again after shutdown.\\n- EOS APIs that need newer engine or EOS SDK versions are now guarded so the plugin builds on older versions."}]}}')}}]);